{
  "id": "ss.relic.vine-thorn",
  "name": "Thornbed",
  "description": "What is left when a vine dies: the runner gone brown and lying across the ground it came out of, with its thorns still standing up out of it. Five of them at uneven heights and leaning apart rather than a tidy row, because a row of equal spikes is a comb and this is a thing that grew and then stopped. The bed is the same soil the weapon's own hole is cut in, and the runner is `$timber.dark` against the plant's moss \u2014 dead wood is the one colour this arsenal already has for something that used to be alive. `$husk` on the thorns for the same reason the weapon's own barbs wear it: bone against green is a thorn, green against green is a bump.",
